#! btw 1
#! name: such stuff as dreams, 122
#! license: CC0-1.0
#! visibility: public
# such-stuff-as-dreams-122: a phrase compiled to a track (CC0-1.0; the words are Shakespeare's, The Tempest 4.1, first printed in
# 1623, in the public domain). `template(deep-house, @tempest_such_stuff)` is deep house at 122 in A minor whose vocal line is the
# verse: twenty syllables of iambic pentameter, each stressed one on a beat and accented, a four-bar line sung twice in every
# eight-bar section. In `night` the voice is buried (lower, darker, ducked under the kick); in `spot` it is up front, an octave
# up the first time and crossed onto the shaker's rhythm the second. The `drm_*` drums fill in a little more each pass; the kick
# and the clap stay put. Four passes, about four minutes. `btwd expand` writes it out as plain BeatScript to edit from there.
arrange from template(deep-house, @tempest_such_stuff)
